Lore of the Fading Summer                                  Development Log
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This mud will serve as a bed for experimentation and streamlining
alongside the mud called Estilore.  My goal with this library is to
replace the current library that Estilore runs on with more modern and
recently written code.  It is understood that the longer a piece of code
exists, the more reliable it will become due to the effects and tests that
time places on it and the inevitable tweaking and reworking that takes
place by those who are using it.  However, I hope to glean what knowledge
I can from the experience I have had using the older library (TMI-2
based) and use that to create a better library.  It is also my hope to be
able to actively maintain this library and to expand on it.

My work begins on June 15, 2001, at 2:26 PM, CST (GMT-6).  I took the Lil
mud library from the MudOS v22.2b11 source.  My goal now is to work out
standards for the mudlib, such as which compile-time options we will
require from the driver and what methods of input-processing will be
relied on (e.g. add_action or natural language parsing).  After having
cleaned up the Lil code a bit and removing the code that supports options
we do not use, I will proceed to create a security system.  Then I will
move on to commands, etc., and continue working until the job is ready to
be submitted to Tal, Finellen, and Cookie, when hopefully they will agree
to move our areas and other things to this mud library.

-Lontau (Dante), 15-06-2001
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

I resume my work today.  The first task I undertook was to remove all the
commands from the Lil mudlib that we did not need.  Now I am beginning
to decide on our directory structure.  After this is done, I will attempt
to implement natural language parsing.  This involves the creation of a
base object for the mudlib and the addition of several new applies to the
master object.

It is my hope that after a lot of work, this mudlib will look nothing like
any other mudlib that exists already.  I also hope it will be the most
efficient and cleanly written mudlib, and that we will all enjoy working
with it.  Whether or not this works out remains to be seen.  This is
actually the second day I have worked on it.

-Lontau, 17-06-2001
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Yesterday saw productivity.  Before going to bed in the early hours of the
morning today, I had successfully implemented natural language parsing and
written one command to use it... "dest".  Today I plan to remove all the
commands from the Lil mudlib and start over from scratch, using parsing
rules instead of complicated routines to find out what the user meant.

Also on the agenda for today is the creation of a daemon to initialize all
the 'verbs', all the commands that will be known to the parser.  This
daemon will also have functions to make it easy to add to and subtract
from the mud's list of verbs. 

-Lontau, 18-06-2001
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the first entry since the project was given a home on SourceForge.
It has been some time since I've made any entries in this file, but I have
been active nonetheless.  Seeing as how most of the entries so far mention
natural language parsing, it seems fitting to now mention that I no longer
desire to use natural language parsing, but instead feel as though a custom
parser is in order.  But as for this project, we are now in the 'Planning'
phase of development, as indicated on SourceForge today.  I am now cleaning
up the code and removing most of the commands, giving us a chance to start
anew.  So far there is only one developer helping me (Faoron).  He and I
will start work on the parser very soon.

-Lontau, 03-07-2001
